{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/783760-let-s-brainstorm-exigents","id":783760,"title":"Let's Brainstorm Exigents!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Exigents"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-10T16:57:34-08:00","id":783760,"title":"Let's Brainstorm Exigents!","content":"So, one of my favorite parts of the new edition are exigents; I've drawn up a few exigent QC's for a game in planning and I'm hoping to crowd source inspiration for more. <br /> <br /> Namely, I'd love to see an Exigent of Ruvia (perhaps through the proxy of a more minor road God, like Revanna is an Exigent of the God of the shining metropolis through a lesser city God)-- what sorts of powers might the God of Roads and Captain of the Golden Barque grant his chosen?<br /> <br /> <br /> Another one I was wondering about would be what a Exigent of Verumpira (Emissary to Malfeas) might look like?<br /> <br /> <br /> I also was wondering what other city God themed exigents would be like and how one might make them distinct form the awesome QC example we have.<br /> <br /> So yeah, feel free to brainstorm with me or share your own ideas","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2116-jivex","name":"JiveX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2116_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T17:34:42-08:00","id":783786,"title":"","content":"One of my favorite Gods is Tien-Yu. I actually LIKE Lookshy, and like Tien-Yu.<br /> <br /> I suppose an Exigent of Tien-Yu with a bit of reined-in power that focuses on combat and a LOT on commanding Battlegroups and Strategic Warfare would be viable. My INITIAL idea required a setting where the Mask decides to destroy Lookshy.<br /> <br /> In the last moments of the city, Tien Yu reveals to a soldier that the Mask has brought Lookshy's end before it was fated to be. So she used her own Essence, combined with the years that the Mask stole from Lookshy, to empower the Exigence. With two commands.<br /> <br /> 1. Buy time for the city to be evacuated.<br /> 2. <b>Make the Mask pay for every inch of Lookshyan soil</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T17:39:23-08:00","id":783791,"title":"","content":"Well, while I probably won't make Exigents before the book comes out, I do have some ideas.<br /> <br /> One of the first concepts I had was a Chosen of Books/Text/Language or some mix thereof, since that's kind of my area (in a modest fashion). That's probably wide enough to make a couple out of, but I've yet to come up with a working layout.<br /> <br /> I've also been thinking about a Chosen of Darkness, who'd have dominion over darkness, shadows and night time and Calibration and appropriate associated metaphorical themes, without (most of) the death themes surrounding Abyssals and (possibly still) Fiends. I'm thinking Five Days Darkness as a patron god?<br /> <br /> Here's a foundational question I've been thinking about in regards to Exigents. When you think about making them, what audience do you imagine, and how does that impact your structure? For example, if you make with the intention that anyone who wants to play a Chosen of X should be able to pick this up and have a reasonable chance of making their vision happen, that's a whole lot different than having a specific path, and maybe even a specific player, in mind for your Exigent. What do you think of as your goal?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T18:25:03-08:00","id":783817,"title":"","content":"Hrm, I don't have any ideas based on canon deities, but I've got a few ruminations.<br /> <br /> I've got an idea for a Pugilist Exalted (Chosen in ancient times by a Southern God of Street Fighting). At the base of their charm set is a martial art style that serves as a particular meditation on violence. The innate Pugilist charms would build off of that. I kind of imagine them as Ability-based, with Charms either geared toward violence or borrowing from that martial art philosophy. Examples might be, a Bureaucracy Charm that aids in backing out of an arrangement (know when to cut and run) or a Linguistics charm that aids blackmail attempts against someone who was originally blackmailing you (Meeting violence with equal violence)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/214-brontes","name":"Brontes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T19:15:30-08:00","id":783851,"title":"","content":"I'm gonna wait for the Exigents book to work it out, but I have an idea for an Exigent of a former god of storms who later became the god of speed. Pretty much an excuse to stat out an expy of The Flash...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T20:45:49-08:00","id":783906,"title":"","content":"How about a drunken master type. Maybe chosen of Burning Feather, Lady of Intoxicants. Or one of her subordinates. Actually, I could see an Exalted stoner work this way too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1047,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","user":"vampire hunter D","date":". 12-11-2015, 04:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T21:58:04-08:00","id":783932,"title":"","content":"I believe Burning Feather is the canon god of drugs. <br /> I second the interest in an Exigent of Verumipra. The writeup says he's uncorrupted by Hell, but pretty powerful; what form does that take? Like, the antithesis of Hellish themes, or maybe the same but in nice colors? So normal-colored brass and flames, gentle darkness and silence, shining sands?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>But sexually.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1797-ellis","name":"Ellis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T22:57:53-08:00","id":783948,"title":"","content":"Does it say what he was god of prior to being sent to Malfeas?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T00:26:47-08:00","id":783980,"title":"","content":"Another vote for Verumipra- I already have a rough concept for his Exigents as some form of &quot;Infernals of Heaven&quot;, that is Chosen with seemingly demonic powers who force Heaven's will upon Hell, yet risk corruption for doing so. Those who become too corrupted are eventually killed and replaced with the new Chosen of Exile.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T00:33:11-08:00","id":783982,"title":"","content":"Ever since I heard of the idea, I've wanted to make an Exigent for Plentimon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Oh boys! Look what I got here!&quot;<br /> &quot;Hey, where the Dynast women at?&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/814-dreamking89","name":"dreamking89","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T00:40:16-08:00","id":783984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/783760-let-s-brainstorm-exigents?p=783851#post783851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm gonna wait for the Exigents book to work it out, but I have an idea for an Exigent of a former god of storms who later became the god of speed. Pretty much an excuse to stat out an expy of The Flash...</div> </div> </div> </div>An Exigent of the god of heliographs, maybe?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T00:52:43-08:00","id":783988,"title":"","content":"I wonder if demons can somehow get a hold of Exigency.<br /> <br /> Because I really want to create an Exigent of Segereth, the Player of Games, or Sondok, Salmalin Supreme!.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;From now on, instead of saying 'half-assed', I will use 'muled'. 'This is a muled job, Chris', I will say to my friend Chris. 'You need to do better, or your ass is grass. And not, like, metaphorical grass. There are weeds growing in there as we speak.'<br /> <br /> &quot;'The DEA is after you, man' I will tell him, in all seriousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8891-khantalas","name":"Khantalas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8891_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"899"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T01:20:08-08:00","id":783996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/783760-let-s-brainstorm-exigents?p=783851#post783851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm gonna wait for the Exigents book to work it out, but I have an idea for an Exigent of a former god of storms who later became the god of speed. Pretty much an excuse to stat out an expy of The Flash...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You know, it's interesting you use that as yourninspirstion, because I always felt Exigents sounded like comic book super heroes. As i it just seemed they'd be based on one power and variatinsmo its use, rather than the wide rangemof abilities true Exalts manage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T03:21:21-08:00","id":784037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khantalas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/783760-let-s-brainstorm-exigents?p=783988#post783988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if demons can somehow get a hold of Exigency.<br /> <br /> Because I really want to create an Exigent of Segereth, the Player of Games, or Sondok, Salmalin Supreme!.</div> </div> </div> </div>From what the devs have said, the Exigence is limited to the gods in-setting, but you can use Exigents as a model for demonic Exalts, and come up with a demonic version of the Exigence..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T13:59:26-08:00","id":784342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/783760-let-s-brainstorm-exigents?p=784037#post784037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> From what the devs have said, the Exigence is limited to the gods in-setting, but you can use Exigents as a model for demonic Exalts, and come up with a demonic version of the Exigence..</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I've toyed with an idea for an Autochthonian equivalent of the Exigence, controlled by the Divine Minsters and given out when they or the people of the Octet need aid or numbers and they don't have time or resources to create a new Champion. I'm considering calling them Synthoids. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JiveX</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another one I was wondering about would be what a Exigent of Verumpira (Emissary to Malfeas) might look like?</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally speaking, I think chains might be some sort of major motif.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JiveX</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also was wondering what other city God themed exigents would be like and how one might make them distinct form the awesome QC example we have.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not a backer, so I'm not quite sure what the idea is up against, but I think that the city's character might be important. For example, a Chosen of Varrang might have Investigation or Occult charms that rely on Astrology to gain information, or a Chosen of Gem (which, if I remember correctly, had a prominent Firedust mine in the previous editions) might have Archery charms optimized around the F tag.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for other ideas, I've considered a Chosen of [Martial Arts Style]. Speaking of which, since I've heard that the Solar charms for Sorcery give you the Thaumaturgy merit, does anyone think that a Brawl charm that grants Martial Artist([Appropriate Style]) would be inappropriate?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T15:11:16-08:00","id":784373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/783760-let-s-brainstorm-exigents?p=784342#post784342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I've toyed with an idea for an Autochthonian equivalent of the Exigence, controlled by the Divine Minsters and given out when they or the people of the Octet need aid or numbers and they don't have time or resources to create a new Champion. I'm considering calling them Synthoids.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>How would that work then? Would they be mechanical like Alchemicals?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T15:27:08-08:00","id":784381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/783760-let-s-brainstorm-exigents?p=784373#post784373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How would that work then? Would they be mechanical like Alchemicals?</div> </div> </div> </div> Personally I'm thinking sort of a cyborg vibe, a human infused with the essence(and quite possibly mind, if the process destroyed them) of a sufficiently powerful and willing Daeva or Elemental. On one hand, the average Synthoid is likely less powerful than a Champion, but it's comparatively easier to find a compatible mortal and potent spirit than it is sinking resources into creating an Alchemical. Mostly just a few ideas at this stage, honestly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T16:54:58-08:00","id":784411,"title":"","content":"Just bumping my question from before, since I'm still curious about it. What scope and audience do you plan to write your Exigents for? Will you tailor them for your group or try to make them viable for anyone to pick up? Will you focus on the expression of a single theme or try to involve several paths that the same Exigent can take?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T20:20:58-08:00","id":784510,"title":"","content":"Once there was a goddess of a lighthouse, who was in love with the house's keeper.<br /> <br /> She wasn't powerful enough to protect her lover from the wrath of an offended Storm Mother - not directly. But pouring all her strength and all her love and everything else she was into a moment of desperate Exigence was enough to create an Exigent capable of guiding people through the dark places of their souls, of granting the light of knowledge, of warning others away from danger, and of course of helping ships navigate...<br /> <br /> ...And of bringing the laser to degrees which have not been seen since Rebuild of Evangelion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u00e4! I\u00e4! Moe fthagn!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/280-valles","name":"Valles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar280_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"677"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-12T03:49:53-08:00","id":784638,"title":"","content":"In our current campaign there is an NPC exigent that the party has made an ally of. Slum Mongrel, the chosen of Savage Roads, Smuggling and Untravelled Paths. The portfolio of his patron, She Eats the Rat Empress, is the concept of crude paths being cut through untamed wilderness that will one day become the heart of cities and supply lines. She doesnt have influence over them once they become safe and established but smuggling routes and secret entrances to things also count. Sewers, eccentric mansion pathways, underground railroads, Mad Max Style supply lines for raiders. Slum Mongrel has charms that make him better at unarmed combat, wrestling, piloting vehicles, detecting hidden pathways both literal and abstract, blessing and fortifying routes so they remain hidden or hard to access and navigating tribal raider cultures.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Exalted: Princes of the Universe<br /> A Third Edition Exalted Podcast<br /> <b><u><a href=\"http://atrusilk.podbean.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://atrusilk.podbean.com/</a></u></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8769-tavelgorge","name":"TavelGorge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8769_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-12T05:58:40-08:00","id":784694,"title":"","content":"I've been toying with the idea of an Exigent of Rahul, the Silver Mirror, who is the city father of Stone, the City of Masks in the Scavenger Lands. I imagine a lot of reflection based powers - some interaction with the intimacy system both within him- or herself and within others, and possibly disguise or power reflection. I imagine a Dragon-Blooded getting the sensation they were fighting against themselves, for instance, or so on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>All that I write but don't cite is simply my perspective, colored by my experiences and beliefs. I extrapolate a lot, too, so don't take it too seriously. :P","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7858-end","name":"*End","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7858_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-12T06:49:38-08:00","id":784707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/783760-let-s-brainstorm-exigents?p=783791#post783791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, while I probably won't make Exigents before the book comes out, I do have some ideas.<br /> <br /> One of the first concepts I had was a Chosen of Books/Text/Language or some mix thereof, since that's kind of my area (in a modest fashion). That's probably wide enough to make a couple out of, but I've yet to come up with a working layout.<br /> <br /> I've also been thinking about a Chosen of Darkness, who'd have dominion over darkness, shadows and night time and Calibration and appropriate associated metaphorical themes, without (most of) the death themes surrounding Abyssals and (possibly still) Fiends. I'm thinking Five Days Darkness as a patron god?<br /> <br /> Here's a foundational question I've been thinking about in regards to Exigents. When you think about making them, what audience do you imagine, and how does that impact your structure? For example, if you make with the intention that anyone who wants to play a Chosen of X should be able to pick this up and have a reasonable chance of making their vision happen, that's a whole lot different than having a specific path, and maybe even a specific player, in mind for your Exigent. What do you think of as your goal?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well if I were to make them<br /> Without a book I would make them just as QC npc's to flesh out the setting","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2116-jivex","name":"JiveX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2116_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-12T12:20:18-08:00","id":784900,"title":"","content":"The first idea I had for an Exigent upon hearing of them was a sort of collaboration among the Great Forks Trio, most likely bestowed upon the mortal daughter of Talespinner. I had some Charm ideas I thought were pretty great based on mixing their domains (hold off Raksha predation with the Magnificent Dream Shield! Inspire armies with the Tale Of Glorious Victory!), but as a little more information trickled out, it turned out that this would actually be a &quot;Dirty Bomb&quot; Exalt, meaning it's (1) not allowed by Heaven, and (2) probably some kind of crazy mutant. Hopefully, either the Exigent book will give me some inspiration to guide this concept back to where I like it, or I'll get more sold on the idea of Great Forks accidentally making a crazy mutant instead of a champion.<br /> <br /> I've also also always been fascinated by the contradiction of the slavery god (Rapsbolga?) - a being who at once embodies the institution and the slaves themselves, and thus must perpetuate his own suffering and seek to break his own will. I'm tickled by the idea of him Exalting some especially willful slave (presumably through the black market rather than the sun's will), and actually being crazy enough to be surprised when this person sets out to end slavery outright. Of course, our would-be hero would have to grapple with his extremely twisted powerset, often fueled by the suffering of himself or others. The social Charms would be especially problematic. Obviously, this design would need to be finessed just right to avoid seeming too Abyssal-ey.<br /> <br /> Inspired by the importance of honey in the ancient world (&quot;the tears of Ra,&quot; as they used to say), I would love an Exigent of a Bee God. I'd probably have the initiating god die, Janest-style, so the Bee Queen can, well, lead the hive. I see her as sort of a reclusive alchemist (bee powers are great at transformation and making gold), but with an ever-larger ragtag city growing up around her - since she both supplies food/protection and has Charms which work best when assisted by many workers.<br /> <br /> ...I'm still not sure I think of those are as cool as the Bleak Warden, though. Warden so good!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T00:24:16-08:00","id":785237,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of the Exigents of the Elemental Dragons.<br /> <br /> Like... <b>The</b> Elemental Dragons.<br /> <br /> ... And yes, I know, technically by the rules that wouldn't work but I kinda... don't care?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T00:47:43-08:00","id":785251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jetstream</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/783760-let-s-brainstorm-exigents?p=785237#post785237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the idea of the Exigents of the Elemental Dragons.<br /> <br /> Like... <b>The</b> Elemental Dragons.<br /> <br /> ... And yes, I know, technically by the rules that wouldn't work but I kinda... don't care?</div> </div> </div> </div>So... how would these Exigents differ from the Dragonblooded?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T15:20:36-08:00","id":785592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/783760-let-s-brainstorm-exigents?p=784411#post784411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just bumping my question from before, since I'm still curious about it. What scope and audience do you plan to write your Exigents for? Will you tailor them for your group or try to make them viable for anyone to pick up? Will you focus on the expression of a single theme or try to involve several paths that the same Exigent can take?</div> </div> </div> </div>If I was making my exigent for someone or for use as an NPC, I'd probably focus on the areas of interest, but I think I'd probably want to make a few notes about other things that the Exigent could theoretically do.<br /> <br /> If I'm doing it as a fan splat and putting it up on the net, I'd want to go for as many options as I think fit that Exigent, because I don't know who'd be using it.<br /> <br /> As for exploring a theme, I think I'd probably stick to exploring the theme of that god, but I'd be trying to explore it in as many ways as was legit.<br /> <br /> Like, I had this idea for the Exigent of Hot Springs, mostly as an excuse for using the Anime Hot Springs Trope and stuff, but, as I thought about it more, the character turned into a Heavenly troubleshooter and geomancer, because the Hot Springs are places where all of the elements meet and their geomancy can be both important to creation and rather fragile. She'd have powers centered around heat, steam, water, geomancy, cleansing, and, yes, Anime Hot Spring Tropes because I wasn't going to just give up that part of the idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T15:41:56-08:00","id":785608,"title":"","content":"Currently, my approach to Exigents is informed by Nobilis, in that the portfolio of the god serves as the conceptual basis and center point for a charmset that is, essentially, a commentary on what that portfolio means. I'm getting a lot of mileage out of Persona, the idea that the properties of your portfolio can be applied to other things.<br /> <br /> I've been thinking on a Plague Exigent who can make ideas and concepts run through a community like a disease, take diseases away, create magical diseases, even create an anti-plague that cures those who get it. Hmmm... If she can make herself immune to diseases, and then redefine, say, &quot;getting stabbed&quot; as a disease, that could be an interesting combo. Possibly tricky to balance. But potentially fun.<br /> <br /> Can become immune to up to Essence diseases. Can define one specific condition that she's currently under as a disease, such as &quot;stabbed by Mnemon,&quot; after which she can not only become immune to further stabbings by Mnemon, but she an also make &quot;Being stabbed by Mnemon&quot; contagious and start spreading it around to everyone.<br /> <br /> I suspect a lot of her functionality is going to be &quot;take this thing I have, apply 'contagious like a plague' to it, release it, ????, Profit.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T16:51:05-08:00","id":785634,"title":"","content":"I cant stop wondering how could be an Exigent from the god of apocalyptic visions <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/278-elyon","name":"Elyon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar278_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T18:27:46-08:00","id":785670,"title":"","content":"I'm working on an exigent for Siakal the western God of war, slaughter and sharks. Some war charms, sail charms and based on a recommendation on Facebook I might be using some lunar charms from the conversion posted by Irked. the words bloodlust, ruthless, and frenzy come to mind. We'll see how it goes. I'm open to suggestion though. <br /> <br /> As far as the intended audience is concerned, I'm really just tailoring the npc for my game and my PCs. If I really like what I end up with I'll consider posting a fleshed out version for others to use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10225-patternspiderman","name":"PatternSpiderman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-18T23:02:55-08:00","id":789124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>While My Guitar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/783760-let-s-brainstorm-exigents?p=785251#post785251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... how would these Exigents differ from the Dragonblooded?</div> </div> </div> </div>I will answer that question once I have the Corebook and Exigent book and have any idea of what the hell I'm doing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-19T04:39:49-08:00","id":789202,"title":"","content":"Setting aside whether you should do it, I think I'd find it tough to think about Exigents for the Elemental Dragons is we don't really know much about the Elemental Dragons.<br /> <br /> I think from what we know you could go with Attribute based Charms, as the Elemental Dragons have a raw and unpolished nature about them and put into those Charms themes of being draconic and a slumbering fanged and clawed beast. That'd get you close to LunarXDragonblooded, the splat, I think (at least if Lunars are as many would like them to be, emphasising beast and monster themes over the idea of all kinds of shapechanging and adaptability).<br /> <br /> If the goal is more like Dragonblooded who can be fresh and young Exalted (Outcaste or Dynast) while being as mighty as an experienced Dynast, and with some areas where they're as strong as Arada, Bhagwei, Cainan or Mond, with a world where Exigence allows lots of small scale groups of Exalted who can be of whatever power level you fancy, without even touching Exigence or designing a whole new Charmset, that seems like tacit permission to simply go <br /> <br /> &quot;The Dragons awake from their slumber and turn their regard to the world. Their attention and power touches a few among the Dragonblooded. Treat these prodigies as able to learn Charms of +2 Essence beyond their Essence score and give them a Supernal Ability each (or whatever makes sense instead).&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-20T19:20:53-08:00","id":790044,"title":"","content":"Like I said, I've got nothing for the powers in particular. That's going to wait on books. The <b>narrative</b> goal, however, is the idea that the Elemental Dragons wake up or at least take notice of the state of creation, are offended at the Dragon Blooded's temerity, and create exalted champions to help remind them of their place.<br /> <br /> Walking embodiments of the things the Immaculates have bastardized as an illustrative lesson.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-21T13:08:12-08:00","id":790446,"title":"","content":"Hmm... Exalted as I see it is more a place where such a person is probably more likely to go &quot;A walking illustrative lesson huh? I can think of much better uses for such power. Well, thanks for the mojo, EDs&quot;.<br /> <br /> Although, on the other hand, any such person who would actually be content being a mere illustrative lesson for the Dragonblooded would probably be the kind of person who would just make them go &quot;Well, now, I feel slightly irritated at this person's lack of ambition and am edging increasingly closer to atheism. I'd better disembowel them, and then go and shake off this funk with some old fashioned Dynast hedonism!&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}